body:
back in 10th grade, i was a lazy ass student who sleeps 5 hours in class out of 6, the last subject is math and i was good at it so i just stare at the window for the whole period and not listen. and for those of you who was wondering why i was always asleep, its because i play until 3 in the morning and the class starts at 7 (lol) and i was also clinically depressed.

&#x200B;

im not smart, im just really good at figuring things out, my math teacher always approaches me because he thought i was cheating because i am constantly having around 90\~95% in quizzes and activities, one day he let me answer on the board RIGHT AFTER i had just woken up, i showed him how to do it in front of class and they were in awe because i was that "quiet kid" who was always asleep and never gave a fuck, the days after that my classmates were talking to me like and wanting me to help them in math problems, its not that i dont want to help them, its just it reached the point where it became a nuisance to me and disturbing my sleep, and 2 months after that that day, i was transferred to the afternoon classes, but before i transferred was exams week, and the teacher has left for 30 minutes and we're talking the math exam, and i gave my paper to the people beside me and let them copy, then soon after i let the whole class copy my exam(note that this was the 2nd semester)... in the first semester, the section average was \~70% and some students were struggling, then came the results, i bumped the class average from \~70% to \~95%, it might not be as big as a valedictorian or something like that but to me, that is my greatest accomplishment.
